# Skill authoring hygiene — warm-up byte budget

**On-demand rule.** Read when authoring or reviewing **`missions/*/skills/*/SKILL.md`** under the software-development center — especially spawn skills subject to the **384 KiB** host spawn cap (`.sedea/centers/sedea/rules/4_mission.mdc` § *Spawned execution*).

## Skill prose size gate (binding — PRD D2)

When a PR **adds or expands** a **`SKILL.md`** body (markdown after frontmatter) so the **on-disk file** exceeds **40 KiB** (40,960 bytes):

1. **Justify on-demand split in the PR description** — name which prose moves to a satellite doc under `missions/<mission>/docs/` or `docs/`, and which **`Read`** hooks in the skill bind those paths at named protocol steps (same pattern as Phase B **`coding-session`** ship-chain docs and Phase C **`spawn-ship-contracts.md`** / **`planning-mode-templates.md`** splits).
2. **Keep frontmatter `warmUpRules` / `laneRules` slim** — heavy tables, spawn preflight rows, and ship-chain procedure belong in on-demand docs unless the path is required on every spawn (see **`missions/plan-and-deliver/skills/README.md`** § *Warm-up cap exceptions*).
3. **Do not** grow monolithic skill bodies to carry verify tables, MCP wire copies, or checkpoint option catalogs that already live in center rules or on-demand docs — link and **`Read`** at step boundaries instead.

**Verification:** `missions/plan-and-deliver/scripts/verify-warmup-bytes.mjs` emits **`WARN:`** when skill body exceeds 40 KiB. **`verify-skill-manifest.mjs`** remains authoritative for the **384 KiB** spawn path budget.

## Spawn path budget (cross-ref)

The **384 KiB** cap applies to deduped frontmatter **`warmUpRules` ∪ `laneRules`** path bodies, excluding the assigned skill body when the host injects **`skillPath`** (lane-manifest-contract § *Spawn cap*). Per-role totals print in CI via **`verify-warmup-bytes.mjs --table`** (PRD D1).

